# A Compile game, written down move by move.
#
# Lines that are not comments are commands, exactly as they are typed at the
# prompt. Undo and redo are moves like any other, so reading this file back
# retraces the game as it was really played - second thoughts and all - and
# arrives at the same position it was saved from.
#
# The deal line says how many were playing, what they were dealt from, and who
# was in each seat - 'you' for a person here, a skill for the program.
#
#   dotnet run -- compile replay <this file>

deal 2 639223667499103342 you you

#   1  turn 1, Player 1
draft water
#      Player 1 drafts Water.

#   2  turn 2, Player 2
draft darkness
#      Player 2 drafts Darkness.

#   3  turn 3, Player 2
draft hate
#      Player 2 drafts Hate.

#   4  turn 4, Player 1
draft fire
#      Player 1 drafts Fire.

#   5  turn 5, Player 1
draft gravity
#      Player 1 drafts Gravity.

#   6  turn 6, Player 2
draft speed
#      Player 2 drafts Speed.
#      The draft is over. Both players now set their 3 protocols against the 3 lines, face down.

#   7  turn 7, Player 1
arrange water fire gravity
#      Player 1 sets Water, Fire, Gravity against lines 1 to 3.

#   8  turn 8, Player 2
arrange hate darkness speed
#      Player 2 sets Hate, Darkness, Speed against lines 1 to 3.
#      Both are turned over at once - Player 1 has Water, Fire, Gravity; Player 2 has Hate, Darkness, Speed.
#      Both decks are shuffled - 18 cards each - and 5 drawn.

#   9  turn 9, Player 1
play fire-4 1 down
#      Player 1 plays Fire-4 face down to line 1, for 2.

#  10  turn 10, Player 2
play hate-3 1
#      Player 2 plays Hate-3 to line 1.

#  11  turn 11, Player 1
play fire-0 2
#      Player 1 plays Fire-0 to line 2.
#      Fire-0 asks Player 1 to choose.

#  12  turn 11, Player 1
choose fire-4
#      Player 1's Fire-4 on line 1 is turned face up.
#      Fire-4 asks Player 1 to choose.

